From 03c14bf54ccc6fc9f1e40ce7b08f318955216660 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ObeseCatLord <6099645+ObeseCatLord@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 12:39:12 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] VR battle table: the stage's map model drawn natively on the
 plate (grid, play area, obstacle solids)

- bvr_assets: AXO line primitives (lines, line strips) are kept as index pairs (Part::lines); Stage::mapModel reads
  MAPVIEW_MAPMODELFILENAME.
- bvr_ships::mapModel(): the identified stage's map model, built on the loader thread (Mesh::Part::lines).
- ga2_vr drawMapModel: the model under the table's own map transform (turned and scaled with the map), lines glowing,
  solids faint glass, heights flattened to 15 % (GA2_MAP_HEIGHT), clipped to the round plate with its rim fade.
  GA2_NATIVE_MAP=0 turns it off (the game then draws the map's 3D as before).

With native/compat/ga2_battledraw.cpp skipping the game's map meshes while the table shows the map, an Eigou 1
battle in table mode runs at full speed with the game thread at 44-46 % (was ~85-95 %); VU1 17.5 Mcycles/s.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
